{%- comment -%}
Renders a duration, preserving the precision the author recorded.

With `precise` set — a route timed to the second — it reads as a race clock:
"1:53:23", or "22:15" under an hour. Otherwise it reads as "1h 53m" or "22m",
so a hike logged to the nearest minute does not claim a ":00" it never had.

Jekyll includes share the caller's scope, so the working names total_seconds,
clock_hours, remainder, clock_minutes and clock_seconds leak to the caller.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign total_seconds = include.seconds | round -%}
{%- assign clock_hours = total_seconds | divided_by: 3600 -%}
{%- assign remainder = total_seconds | modulo: 3600 -%}
{%- assign clock_minutes = remainder | divided_by: 60 -%}
{%- assign clock_seconds = remainder | modulo: 60 -%}

{%- if include.precise -%}
  {%- if clock_hours > 0 -%}
    {{- clock_hours }}:{{ clock_minutes | prepend: "0" | slice: -2, 2 }}:{{ clock_seconds | prepend: "0" | slice: -2, 2 -}}
  {%- else -%}
    {{- clock_minutes }}:{{ clock_seconds | prepend: "0" | slice: -2, 2 -}}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- if clock_hours > 0 -%}{{ clock_hours }}h {% endif -%}{{ clock_minutes }}m
{%- endif -%}
